35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems my worries were justified. I found that projects based on comfort or appeal often slip by a year or more, and weather has cost us six weeks recently. We must be very careful with our timelines.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Wow, that's a lot of lost time! @Shizue, thank you for sharing. I found something worrying too; we have plenty of specialist rooms sitting empty, but we're constantly turning away requests for general rooms!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings are quite specific. While some newer staff have capacity, our bench technicians are burdened by tedious manual routines, such as window-opening, because our current equipment is insufficient. We must prioritize automation to relieve them.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My findings echo the need for a broader perspective. Post-occupancy reviews show that projects benefiting a single wing are poorly rated, while shared, bookable spaces are highly valued. Also, hazardous materials in older blocks are causing significant delays.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings suggest a rather precarious financial landscape. Mechanical and plant costs have surged by twenty percent, yet our records show a curious absence of renewal reserves for audiovisual equipment. We are planning for tomorrow with yesterday's prices.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is quite concerning to hear all this. @Benjamin, if costs are rising and @Mizuki mentions hazardous materials, I fear our schedules will slip even further. We must choose a plan that is simple and predictable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"I agree! But we also have to think about the space. I found that whenever a room is closed for work, we have to pay for off-site space! That sounds so expensive and stressful for everyone involved.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, that is a valid point, but we must not forget that the ""stress"" is felt most acutely by the technicians. If we choose a plan that ignores their manual burdens, we are simply shifting the cost to our people.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I understand, but we must avoid creating a ""silo"" solution. My data shows that narrow, wing-specific improvements are the least successful. We need a plan that relieves staff while providing high-utility, shared value for the whole campus.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is fascinating how we all discover different flavors of dysfunction. @George, while I sympathize with the technicians, we must acknowledge that automation requires the very mechanical plant costs that are currently skyrocketing. We cannot simply wish for efficiency.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is a bit overwhelming, isn't it? @Benjamin, @George, please don't argue. Perhaps we can find a path that is modest in scope to avoid those costly surprises and keep our promises on the calendar.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"I agree with @Shizue! We should look for a plan that doesn't make the timetable a nightmare. If we can find something that gives us more general-purpose rooms without closing too many others, everyone would be so happy!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"I am not arguing, @Shizue, merely ensuring we are honest about the human cost. @Benjamin, if costs are rising, it is all the more reason to invest in systems that reduce manual labor now, rather than paying for inefficiency forever.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, while I agree on reducing labor, we must be strategic. If we invest in a specialized system that only serves one area, we repeat past mistakes. We need a solution that is both efficient and accessible to all.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@George, your passion is admirable, but investing in inefficiency is not the same as investing in a budget deficit. If we ignore the twenty percent surge in plant costs, we are merely painting a crumbling wall.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"Let us all take a deep breath. It seems we are all very passionate because we care. Perhaps we can look for a candidate that is essential for safety or compliance, as those seem to stay on schedule.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"That's a good idea, @Shizue! But let's also make sure the plan doesn't leave us with no place to teach. I really hope we can find a balance that helps the staff and the students!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"I agree with @Shizue. A plan focused on essential infrastructure or safety often provides the most stability. However, I will support any candidate that specifically addresses the manual burdens of our technicians.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree with @Shizue. A focus on essential infrastructure is wise, provided it doesn't create a silo. Let's prioritize a plan that is safe, budget-conscious, and offers shared utility to avoid the disappointments of the past.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"A most prudent conclusion, @Shizue. If we seek a plan that is both fiscally honest and operationally stable, we must avoid the siren song of ""innovation"" that ignores current market inflation. Let us see which candidates survive this scrutiny.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
